From c9c3b3e2fa703fa34a4b405191a939e3b24e6719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xCollxn <81695022+xCollxn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:40:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Add DacaiDriver for Creality DACAI panels (e.g. Ender 3
 Max Neo)

DACAI panels emulate most of the T5UIC1 protocol. DacaiDriver handles the
measured differences:

- SRAM JPEGs are drawn with 0x70 (0x24 is not implemented).
- 0x27 bit 7 is inverted (set = black transparent).
- 0x33 stores the whole 32 KB SRAM as image/<id>.jpg and needs FF D9 at the
  end: JPEGs are padded with a COM segment; picture IDs above 15 work.
- Icon files cannot be written over UART: the icon library is packed onto
  272x480 JPEG sprite sheets (16 px grid, 4:2:0), uploaded once into
  pictures 16+ with SHA-256 checkpoints in Data Flash (0x0600) and drawn
  with 0x25 + 0x27. 0x28 animations are stepped by the host from the UI
  tick. NFC approach frames are skipped (no auxiliary UART).
- Bare A5 OK Data-Flash acknowledgements are accepted.
- 0x30 is clamped to 0..63; 0..255 is mapped to 4..63.
- Optional faster host link via 0x38 (PETREL_DACAI_BAUD) with fallback,
  reset on close and two-speed probing while waiting for the panel.

tools/dacai_artwork.py re-uploads all artwork after a panel microSD update.
